That's all well and good, but quite beyond the original point--the question
was not "white magic" vs. "black magic", but "lawful wizard" vs. "chaotic
wizard".  My query was meant to be along the lines of, "Why do you think a
lawful wizard is necessarilly a white wizard?"  Lawful and good are not the
same thing (NHINDND, but it does share this aspect): lawful means following
rules, rituals, etc. fairly stringently, while chaotic means doing what
seems best at the time; it's very possible to have lawful evil, chaotic
good, etc.

Granted, in NH, the line is sometimes a little blurry; knights are assumed
to always be lawful good, for instance.  However, elves are always chaotic,
though definitely not always evil.



